  "id": "self-construal",
  "term": "self-construal",
  "definition": "Self-construal is a person’s own understanding of who they are and how they experience themselves. It is often described as either more independent, with the self defined mainly by personal inner qualities, or more interdependent, with the self defined through relationships and social context.",
